      "Provide the avatar, offer, and brand direction rather than asking the builder to guess them.\n4.2 The first screen must explain the business\nThe source stresses that the first screen, or above-the-fold area, should contain the essentials:\n- Headline.\n- Supporting subheadline.\n- Primary call to action.\nA visitor should not have to scroll to discover what the business sells or why it might matter.",
      "A practical test is the loud-bar test:\nIf you said the headline and tagline to someone in a loud bar, would they immediately understand what the business does and why it matters?",
